# Screenshot harness outputs (PNG captures and JSON critique results are transient
# dev-only artifacts). The top-level .md audit outputs are committed; everything
# else (date-stamped capture subdirs, PNG/JSON/HTML artifacts) is ignored.
#
# Pattern rationale:
#   */        — ignores all date-stamped capture subdirectories (e.g. 2026-06-04/)
#   *.png     — ignores all screenshot captures at any nesting depth
#   *.json    — ignores all per-screen critique findings JSON files
#   *.html    — ignores generated contact-sheet HTML (contact_sheet.html)
#
# The committed top-level docs are the audit outputs:
#   gap_register.md        — baseline audit output (EVAL-03 / PROOF-03)
#   gap_register_final.md  — final-pass audit output
#   contact_sheet_index.md — index for the generated contact sheet
# None of these are matched by the rules above (they live at the top level, not
# under a */ subdir, and .md is not in the *.png/*.json/*.html set). gap_register.md
# is additionally negated below to override a *.md rule if one were ever added.

*/
*.png
*.json
*.html
!gap_register.md
